0d1-5666-9116-5d6a99c6b6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-670" :question/problem "Simplify ${({2}^{2})}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the exponents and then we calculate the resulting power of \n$2.$\n:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({2}^{2})}^{3} & = \\\\ {2}^{(2\\cdot 3)} & = \\\\ {2}^{6} & = \\\\ 64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
